@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean
@decl rightV_types_del_eq
-- L4DEL: title: Split the opposite side into changed neighbor types and unchanged non-neighbor types
-- L4DEL: intuition: After deleting all edges incident to a left-side vertex `u`, every right-side neighbor has its type transformed by `typeDrop`, while every right-side non-neighbor keeps its original type. The equality records those two multisets separately.
-- L4DEL: step: Bipartiteness ensures deleting `u`'s incidence set cannot otherwise alter a right-side vertex's degree profile.
-- L4DEL: step: Filtering the right part into neighbors and non-neighbors converts the pointwise type formula into a multiset sum.
