@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean
@decl S_multiset_eq
-- L4DEL: title: Descending degree induction recovers each neighboring-type multiset
-- L4DEL: intuition: The balance equation involving `S_G`, `S_H`, and `typeDrop` forces `S_G = S_H`. Type dropping strictly lowers the first coordinate, so the equality can be solved from the highest degrees downward.
-- L4DEL: step: Degree-zero vertices have empty neighbor-type multisets and form the immediate base case.
-- L4DEL: step: Otherwise every type in either multiset has positive first coordinate; the generic multiset lemma cancels their strictly lower dropped images by descending induction.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/graph_reconstruction.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = equality of the type-profile counts can be proved by descending induction on the first coordinate of t

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean
@decl typeProfile
-- L4DEL: title: The multiset of full vertex types around one vertex
-- L4DEL: intuition: `typeProfile G x` maps the vertex-type invariant `τ G` over every neighbor of `x`. Compared with `degreeProfile`, it remembers both each neighbor's degree and that neighbor's own surrounding degree multiset.
-- L4DEL: step: The profile remains unlabeled: it records which types occur and with what multiplicity, not the identities of their carriers.
-- L4DEL: step: Equality of these profiles under the matching bijection is the last invariant needed before reconstructing adjacency.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/graph_reconstruction.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = The type profile of u is the multiset of the types of its neighbors

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean
@decl count_typeProfile_eq_one_iff_adj
-- L4DEL: title: Distinct vertex types turn profile membership into adjacency
-- L4DEL: intuition: If every vertex type in `G` is distinct, the type of `y` appears exactly once in the type profile of `x` precisely when `x` is adjacent to `y`. No other neighbor can impersonate `y` by carrying the same type.
-- L4DEL: step: Adjacency inserts `y` into `x`'s neighbor set and therefore inserts `τ G y` into the mapped multiset.
-- L4DEL: step: Conversely, an occurrence comes from some neighbor with that type; pairwise distinctness identifies that neighbor with `y`.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/graph_reconstruction.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = Since types are pairwise distinct, adjacency is determined by type profiles

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean
@decl adjacency_preserved_left
-- L4DEL: title: Type and type-profile preservation force adjacency preservation from the left side
-- L4DEL: intuition: For a left-part vertex `x`, equality of type profiles and pointwise preservation of `τ` show that `y` occurs as a neighbor of `x` exactly when `f y` occurs as a neighbor of `f x`.
-- L4DEL: step: Distinct types make `τ G y` a unique marker for `y` inside `typeProfile G x`.
-- L4DEL: step: Transporting that marker through the profile equality and the bijection gives the corresponding adjacency statement in `H`.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/graph_reconstruction.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = τK (b) ∈ TK (a)

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean
@decl type_preserving_bijection_is_iso
-- L4DEL: title: Upgrade the card-matching bijection to a bipartite graph isomorphism
-- L4DEL: intuition: A vertex bijection that preserves both partition sides, all vertex types, and the matched incidence-deleted cards must preserve every edge. The proof packages that adjacency equivalence with the side-preservation witnesses as a `BipartiteIso`.
-- L4DEL: step: Neighboring-type multisets agree for left-side vertices, so adjacency from the left side is preserved.
-- L4DEL: step: Symmetry handles edges presented from the right, while bipartiteness rules out right-to-right pairs; the resulting relation isomorphism uses the original bijection `f`.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written graph-reconstruction proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/graph_reconstruction.pdf
