-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = suppose that its two maximal monomials are

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl ideal_carrier_eq_union
-- L4DEL: title: A type-two pure ideal is the union of two principal divisor sets
-- L4DEL: intuition: Once `m₁` and `m₂` are known to be all the maximal monomials, every monomial in the order ideal divides one of them. The carrier is therefore exactly `divisorsFinset(m₁) ∪ divisorsFinset(m₂)`; Lean writes the two applications with spaces.
-- L4DEL: step: Downward closure puts every divisor of either maximum into the carrier.
-- L4DEL: step: Finiteness guarantees that every carrier element lies below some maximal element; the pair equality leaves only `m₁` or `m₂`.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = Every element of a finite order ideal lies below a maximal element

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl exists_single_greater_var
-- L4DEL: title: Equal-degree distinct triples can be oriented around one exceptional coordinate
-- L4DEL: intuition: For two distinct three-variable monomials of equal total degree, the proof may order the pair so that the second exponent is larger at one coordinate `x` and no larger at either other coordinate. The Lean disjunction records the two possible orientations instead of silently swapping names.
-- L4DEL: step: Equal total degree says the three coordinate differences sum to zero.
