@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl reduced_monomial
-- L4DEL: title: The residual monomial after removing the exceptional-coordinate shift
-- L4DEL: intuition: Given oriented maxima `m₁,m₂` and the exceptional coordinate `x`, `reduced_monomial` lowers the `x` exponent of `m₂` by `m₁(x)+1` and leaves its other exponents unchanged. Its degree is correspondingly reduced by the same shift.
-- L4DEL: step: At `x`, the exponent becomes `m₂(x)-m₁(x)-1`.
-- L4DEL: step: Away from `x`, the exponent remains `m₂(y)`, matching the manuscript's `M_red` construction.
