-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = Then |Mred | = e − c.

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl pureOSeq_decomposition
-- L4DEL: title: Split the union's degree count into a principal sequence and a shifted residual sequence
-- L4DEL: intuition: The degree-`d` monomials below `m₁` contribute the first summand. Monomials below `m₂` but not `m₁` exist only when `d ≥ m₁(x)+1`; subtracting that amount in coordinate `x` bijects them with degree-`d-(m₁(x)+1)` divisors of the reduced monomial.
-- L4DEL: step: A filter-and-cardinality identity first separates the union into the first divisor set and the nonoverlapping part of the second.
-- L4DEL: step: The exceptional-coordinate bijection turns that second part into the shifted residual count, producing the manuscript's equation (2).
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
