-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = ∆F (d) = F (d) − F (d − 1) (d > 0),

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl diff2
-- L4DEL: title: The second backward difference of an integer-valued sequence
-- L4DEL: intuition: At a positive index, `diff2(h,d)` (Lean: `diff2 h d`) measures how the first difference changes: `Δh(d)-Δh(d-1)`. This discrete curvature is the quantity bounded by `1` for each principal sequence and by `2` for their sum.
-- L4DEL: step: The definition reuses `diff`, so its boundary convention is inherited consistently.
-- L4DEL: step: Positive second difference marks local convexity of the discrete sequence; the proof isolates its only critical values.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = ∆2 F (d) = ∆F (d) − ∆F (d − 1) (d > 0).

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl diff2_h_seq_le_one
-- L4DEL: title: A single monomial's degree-count sequence has second difference at most one
-- L4DEL: intuition: For every three-variable monomial and degree, the discrete second difference of its divisor-count sequence is at most `1`. This is the uniform curvature bound obtained from the companion's explicit seven-indicator box-count formula.
