@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl H_seq_diff2_reduction
-- L4DEL: title: Shift a critical second-difference-one bound back one degree
-- L4DEL: intuition: When the second difference at `d+1` equals `1`, an upper bound at `d+1` by the square of its first difference implies the required bound at `d-1`. This is the formal version of the companion's shift reduction (13).
-- L4DEL: step: `H_seq_identity` rewrites the earlier value using the later value and the two neighbouring first differences.
-- L4DEL: step: The second-difference-one equation says those first differences differ by exactly one, so the later square completes to the earlier square.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = If ∆2 H(d + 1) = 1 and H(d + 1) ≤ (∆H(d + 1))2 , then H(d − 1) ≤ (∆H(d))2 .

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_5.lean
@decl sum_log_concave_helper
-- L4DEL: title: The principal-plus-shifted-residual sequence is log-concave
-- L4DEL: intuition: Under the exceptional-coordinate orientation and equal-degree hypotheses, the complete finite-difference case analysis proves log-concavity of the decomposed sequence through the common degree of `m₁` and `m₂`.
-- L4DEL: step: The second-difference bound disposes of nonpositive curvature and reduces positive curvature to values `1` and `2`.
