@file APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean
@decl Erdos138.W_not_guarantee
-- L4DEL: title: One less than a positive van der Waerden number is a counterexample length
-- L4DEL: intuition: When `W k≠0`, minimality gives `W k-1∉monoAP_guarantee_set 2 k`.
-- L4DEL: step: Natural-number arithmetic gives `W k-1<W k`; `not_in_set_of_lt_sInf` then excludes membership in the forcing set.
-- L4DEL: source: Pinned AlphaProof Nexus Lean proof for Erdős 138 = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean#L859-L862

@file APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean
@decl Erdos138.W_diff_bound_gt0
-- L4DEL: title: The quantitative gap bound when `W(k)` is positive
-- L4DEL: intuition: For `k>0` and `W k≠0`, the proof establishes `W(k+1)-W(k)≥k`.
-- L4DEL: step: Minimality supplies a `k`-progression-free colouring through `W k-1`; `not_guarantee_extend` extends it through `(W k-1)+k` without a `(k+1)`-progression.
-- L4DEL: step: That extended counterexample lies strictly below `W(k+1)`, and natural-number arithmetic rearranges the inequality into the desired difference bound.
-- L4DEL: source: Pinned AlphaProof Nexus Lean proof for Erdős 138 = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean#L864-L868
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written proof companion for Erdős 138 = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/ErdosProblems/erdos138.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written proof companion for Erdős 138 = We will show that W(k + 1) ≥ W(k) + k

@file APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean
@decl Erdos138.W_diff_ge_k
-- L4DEL: title: The gap bound for every natural `k`
-- L4DEL: intuition: For all natural numbers `k`, `W(k+1)-W(k)≥k`, including the edge cases introduced by the natural-number encoding.
-- L4DEL: step: The case `k=0` is immediate. If `k>0` but `W k=0`, the proof first shows that the empty interval cannot force a positive-length progression and extends that counterexample.
-- L4DEL: step: When `W k≠0`, the result is exactly `W_diff_bound_gt0`.
-- L4DEL: source: Pinned AlphaProof Nexus Lean proof for Erdős 138 = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean#L870-L897
