@file APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean
@decl Erdos138.W_diff_ge_k_all
-- L4DEL: title: The pointwise lower bound used to prove divergence
-- L4DEL: intuition: This wrapper presents the uniform inequality `k≤W(k+1)-W(k)` in the orientation expected by `Filter.tendsto_atTop_mono`.
-- L4DEL: step: At zero the bound is trivial; at a successor it invokes `W_diff_ge_k` with the positive index.
-- L4DEL: step: The AlphaProof Nexus paper also records Thomas Bloom's off-diagonal generalization; that is linked as context, not claimed by this Lean declaration.
-- L4DEL: source: Pinned AlphaProof Nexus Lean proof for Erdős 138 = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean#L898-L901
