@decl socleDegree
-- L4DEL: title: The shared total degree of a pure ideal's maximal monomials
-- L4DEL: intuition: `socleDegree(P)` (Lean: `socleDegree P`) chooses one maximal monomial and returns its total degree. Purity proves that every other maximal monomial has the same degree, so the result is independent of which witness is chosen.
-- L4DEL: step: Nonemptiness of the maximal set supplies the chosen witness.
-- L4DEL: step: The socle degree is the top index through which unimodality or log-concavity is asserted.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = this common degree is the socle degree.

@decl pureOSequence
-- L4DEL: title: Degree-by-degree counts of monomials in an order ideal
-- L4DEL: intuition: `pureOSequence(I,d)` (Lean: `pureOSequence I d`) counts the monomials in `I` whose total degree is exactly `d`. Varying `d` produces the Hilbert-function sequence studied by the theorem.
-- L4DEL: step: The carrier is filtered by the equation `totalDeg m = d`.
-- L4DEL: step: The cardinality of that filtered finite set is the value of the sequence at degree `d`.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: source: Richard P. Stanley, Hilbert functions of graded algebras (1978) = https://math.mit.edu/~rstan/pubs/pubfiles/30.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = The pure O-sequence of Γ is hΓ (d) = #{m ∈ Γ : |m| = d}.
-- L4DEL: quote: Richard P. Stanley, Hilbert functions of graded algebras (1978) = is said to be an O-sequence if there exists an order ideal M of monomials

@decl IsLogConcaveUpTo
-- L4DEL: title: Log-concavity at every internal degree through a chosen endpoint
-- L4DEL: intuition: `IsLogConcaveUpTo(e,h)` (Lean: `IsLogConcaveUpTo e h`) requires `h(i-1)·h(i+1) ≤ h(i)²` for every integer index strictly between `0` and `e`. Each middle term must therefore dominate the geometric mean of its two neighbours.
-- L4DEL: step: `Finset.Ioo 0 e` makes both boundary exclusions explicit: neither `0` nor `e` is tested.
-- L4DEL: step: For the pure O-sequence theorem, `e` is instantiated with the socle degree.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = hΓ (i − 1)hΓ (i + 1) ≤ hΓ (i)2 (0 < i < e).

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry/hilbert_functions_3.lean
@decl Monomial
-- L4DEL: title: A monomial as its vector of natural-number exponents
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Lean type `Monomial(r)` is the finitely supported exponent vector for a monomial in `r` variables. For the manuscript's three-variable theorem, a monomial such as `x₀^a x₁^b x₂^c` is therefore represented by the vector `(a,b,c)` in `ℕ³`.
-- L4DEL: step: A coordinate records the exponent of one variable, so comparing two values pointwise is the same divisibility order used throughout the proof.
-- L4DEL: step: The Lean definition works for any finite number `r` of variables; the companion specializes this representation to `r = 3`.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = the exponent vector m = (m(0), m(1), m(2)) ∈ N3

@decl totalDeg
-- L4DEL: title: Total degree is the sum of a monomial's exponents
-- L4DEL: intuition: `totalDeg(m)`—written `totalDeg m` in Lean—adds every coordinate of the exponent vector. In three variables this is `m(0)+m(1)+m(2)`, the usual total degree of the represented monomial.
-- L4DEL: step: The finitely supported sum makes the definition uniform in the number of variables.
-- L4DEL: step: Degree is the grading used both to group the order ideal into its O-sequence and to state that all maximal monomials of a pure ideal lie in one degree.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = |m| = m(0) + m(1) + m(2) for total degree.

@decl OrderIdeal
-- L4DEL: title: A finite set of monomials closed downward under divisibility
-- L4DEL: intuition: An `OrderIdeal(r)` (Lean: `OrderIdeal r`) stores a finite collection of monomials together with the guarantee that every divisor of a stored monomial is stored too. In exponent-vector form, divisibility is coordinatewise `≤`.
-- L4DEL: step: `carrier` is the finite set itself.
-- L4DEL: step: `downward_closed` is the proof that if `n` is in the carrier and `m ≤ n`, then `m` is also in it.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: source: Richard P. Stanley, Hilbert functions of graded algebras (1978) = https://math.mit.edu/~rstan/pubs/pubfiles/30.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = A finite order ideal Γ ⊂ N3 is a finite set closed downward under this order
-- L4DEL: quote: Richard P. Stanley, Hilbert functions of graded algebras (1978) = is said to be an O-sequence if there exists an order ideal M of monomials

@decl divisorsFinset
-- L4DEL: title: All monomial divisors of one generator as a finite set
-- L4DEL: intuition: `divisorsFinset(g)` (Lean: `divisorsFinset g`) is the principal lower set of `g`: it contains exactly the monomials `u` whose exponent vector is coordinatewise at most that of `g`. Equivalently, these are the monomial divisors of `g`.
-- L4DEL: step: In the type-two proof, every element of the pure order ideal lies below one of its two maximal monomials.
-- L4DEL: step: This lets the carrier be rewritten as the union of two such divisor sets, the first combinatorial reduction in the manuscript proof.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = Div(g) = {u : u ≤ g}.

@decl IsMaximalIn
-- L4DEL: title: Maximality inside an order ideal under monomial divisibility
-- L4DEL: intuition: `IsMaximalIn(I,m)` (Lean: `IsMaximalIn I m`) says first that `m` belongs to `I`, and then that no strictly larger monomial of `I` is divisible by `m`. Any member `n` above `m` must also lie below `m`, hence equals it in the partial order.
-- L4DEL: step: The condition is relative to the selected order ideal, not maximality among all monomials.
-- L4DEL: step: These maximal elements are the generators whose shared degree and number determine purity, socle degree, and type.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = A monomial m ∈ Γ is maximal if every n ∈ Γ with m ≤ n also satisfies n ≤ m.

@decl IsPure
-- L4DEL: title: Purity means every maximal monomial has the same total degree
-- L4DEL: intuition: `IsPure(I)` (Lean: `IsPure I`) requires any two maximal monomials of `I` to have equal total degree. It does not itself assert that a maximal monomial exists; that nonemptiness is added by `PureOrderIdeal`.
-- L4DEL: step: The equal-degree condition supplies one common top grading for the ideal.
-- L4DEL: step: That common degree becomes the socle degree used as the endpoint of the finite O-sequence.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = The ideal is pure if all maximal monomials have the same total degree

@decl PureOrderIdeal
-- L4DEL: title: An order ideal packaged with purity and a maximal monomial
-- L4DEL: intuition: `PureOrderIdeal(r)` (Lean: `PureOrderIdeal r`) is the structure used when later statements need a pure finite order ideal as data. It contains the ideal, a proof that its maximal monomials share one degree, and a proof that the maximal set is nonempty.
-- L4DEL: step: The nonempty field makes the subsequent choice of a maximal monomial—and therefore the definition of socle degree—total rather than conditional.
-- L4DEL: step: This is a formal packaging choice around the manuscript's mathematical notion of a pure order ideal, not a stronger log-concavity assertion.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = The ideal is pure if all maximal monomials have the same total degree

@decl typePO
-- L4DEL: title: The type is the number of maximal monomials
-- L4DEL: intuition: `typePO(P)` is the cardinality of `maximalMonomials(P.ideal)`. In Lean these are written `typePO P` and `maximalMonomials P.ideal`. Thus “type 2” in the theorem means that the pure order ideal has exactly two maximal monomial generators.
-- L4DEL: step: The definition counts maximal monomials; it does not count variables, degrees, or all elements of the ideal.
-- L4DEL: step: The main proof uses type two to name two distinct maxima and express the carrier as the union of their divisor sets.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = The type is the number of maximal monomials.

@decl socleDegree
-- L4DEL: title: The shared total degree of a pure ideal's maximal monomials
-- L4DEL: intuition: `socleDegree(P)` (Lean: `socleDegree P`) chooses one maximal monomial and returns its total degree. Purity proves that every other maximal monomial has the same degree, so the result is independent of which witness is chosen.
-- L4DEL: step: Nonemptiness of the maximal set supplies the chosen witness.
-- L4DEL: step: The socle degree is the top index through which unimodality or log-concavity is asserted.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = this common degree is the socle degree.

@decl pureOSequence
-- L4DEL: title: Degree-by-degree counts of monomials in an order ideal
-- L4DEL: intuition: `pureOSequence(I,d)` (Lean: `pureOSequence I d`) counts the monomials in `I` whose total degree is exactly `d`. Varying `d` produces the Hilbert-function sequence studied by the theorem.
-- L4DEL: step: The carrier is filtered by the equation `totalDeg m = d`.
-- L4DEL: step: The cardinality of that filtered finite set is the value of the sequence at degree `d`.
