-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = The pure O-sequence of Γ is hΓ (d) = #{m ∈ Γ : |m| = d}.
-- L4DEL: quote: Richard P. Stanley, Hilbert functions of graded algebras (1978) = is said to be an O-sequence if there exists an order ideal M of monomials

@decl IsLogConcaveUpTo
-- L4DEL: title: Log-concavity at every internal degree through a chosen endpoint
-- L4DEL: intuition: `IsLogConcaveUpTo(e,h)` (Lean: `IsLogConcaveUpTo e h`) requires `h(i-1)·h(i+1) ≤ h(i)²` for every integer index strictly between `0` and `e`. Each middle term must therefore dominate the geometric mean of its two neighbours.
-- L4DEL: step: `Finset.Ioo 0 e` makes both boundary exclusions explicit: neither `0` nor `e` is tested.
-- L4DEL: step: For the pure O-sequence theorem, `e` is instantiated with the socle degree.
-- L4DEL: source: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/0647711a71183c1ea492ad60860776617ce1ea88/NaturalLanguageProofs/AICollaborator/hilbert.pdf
-- L4DEL: quote: Human-written Hilbert-functions proof companion = hΓ (i − 1)hΓ (i + 1) ≤ hΓ (i)2 (0 < i < e).

