-- L4DEL: intuition: The index condition on $(j, k)$ from the conjecture: $0 < \min\{2,k\} \le j \le k$. Since j and k are natural numbers, $0 < \min\{2,k\}$ is equivalent to $1 \le k$.

@file APNOutputs/OEIS/oeis_113254_conjecture_0.lean
@decl a
-- L4DEL: title: A113254: Corresponds to $m = 8$ in a family of 4th-order linear recurrence sequences
-- L4DEL: intuition: A113254: Corresponds to $m = 8$ in a family of 4th-order linear recurrence sequences. The sequence $a(n)$ is defined by the initial conditions $a(0)=-1, a(1)=4, a(2)=176, a(3)=3136$, and the linear recurrence relation $a(n) = -4 * a (n-1) + 256 * a (n-3) + 4096 * a (n-4)$ for $n \ge 4$.

