@file APNOutputs/OEIS/oeis_278070_conjecture_0.lean
@decl A278070
-- L4DEL: title: A278070: $a(n) = \text{hypergeometric}([n, -n], [], -1)$
-- L4DEL: intuition: A278070: $a(n) = \text{hypergeometric}([n, -n], [], -1)$. This is equivalent to the combinatorial sum: $$a(n) = \sum_{k=0}^n \binom{n}{k} \binom{n+k-1}{k} k!$$ The expression uses $\mathbb{N}$ arithmetic throughout, safely handling the subtraction via `Nat.pred`.

